ther princes, and the famous Bharata and Yuddhajit* and Sumantra and others that are engaged in our welfare. *One of the counsellors.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.896,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-81-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2075011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"97bbe84bf4344ce277bcd4d18ea55690d4002f55613e5787595db4b7f3006e15","compact":"aadec8094d0fd9bdf351d4f1295eabcca2af7617d41c77f69f62befa4dec50f4","nasal":"aadec8094d0fd9bdf351d4f1295eabcca2af7617d41c77f69f62befa4dec50f4"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-75-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":75,"verse":12,"english":"Then there arose a mighty hubbub occasioned by people coming up in cars, horses and elephants.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-81-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2075012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a272b85e96470ea60bb459622d40dbd86815a8556194416986db7255dcf91824","compact":"7f6cdfc10adaf90e9c7ecc83a5bdc6312a9e38f57667b570d9189987b6b4422e","nasal":"7f6cdfc10adaf90e9c7ecc83a5bdc6312a9e38f57667b570d9189987b6b4422e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-75-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":75,"verse":13,"english":"When Bharata arrived, the subjects rejoiced as they used to rejoice on Daſaratha's arrival; and as rejoiced the immortals on the arrival of him of an hundred sacrifices.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-81-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2075013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9d8d385cf310c826fc77167f432de9b0c8c460625e51c919cc15d97000089a9b","compact":"ac313ffb5213f2421910f208a4abd475f39565294cc307d1dccee54e95827dcf","nasal":"73b8fedfef1b9babde0d7ac636b907cd47ea9a841